{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"AC1 verified: PR #131 is still OPEN and current (checked 2026-08-19; branch dependabot/uv/uv-lock-4320b5f53c, updated 2026-08-19T21:51:02Z). It is the ONLY open PR on navapbc/rebar, so nothing has superseded it. origin/main still carries the old pins (ruff==0.16.2, botocore 1.43.70, genai-prices 0.1.2, json-repair 0.63.1, mypy 2.3.0), confirming the bump has not already landed.\n\nFINDING — resolved versions are AHEAD of the PR's pins. Regenerating the lock with the project's uv workflow (`uv lock --upgrade-package` scoped to exactly the five grouped packages) resolves:\n\n  botocore      1.43.70 -> 1.43.75   (PR named 1.43.72)\n  genai-prices  0.1.2   -> 0.1.4     (PR named 0.1.3)\n  json-repair   0.63.1  -> 0.63.3    (PR named 0.63.2)\n  mypy          2.3.0   -> 2.3.1     (matches)\n  ruff          0.16.2  -> 0.16.3    (matches)\n\nUpstream released further patches while the PR sat unlanded. Taking the current resolution rather than pinning back to the PR's exact versions, on the ticket's own guidance that re-pinning past what upstream has moved to 'actively fights dependabot' — holding the lock behind the resolver would invite an immediate follow-up PR. The five packages named in AC2 are all bumped; three land one to three patches further ahead. No packages added or removed; diff is +81/-73 on uv.lock, exactly the stat the PR reported."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787191899585441001,"uuid":"891d6f88-6957-4e08-8c33-8f18c2feea1b"}